course: dictionary
lesson: 2071
title: Old names of places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A place can have more than one name over time. Constantinople is the old name of a great city that is now called Istanbul, in Turkey.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «The Ottoman sultan Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453, ending the Byzantine Empire.» Captured tells you it was a city, and the year 1453 tells you it happened long ago. So Constantinople is the name of a place from the past.
explain: Games and maps often use modern or English names, while people at the time used other names. When you meet a place name you do not know, check the clues around it, then use a dictionary or a map to be sure.
fact: Constantinople was the old name of the city now called Istanbul, in Turkey.
fact: It was the capital of the Eastern Roman (Byzantine) Empire and later of the Ottoman Empire.
fact: «The empire was split into a western half ruled from Rome and an eastern half ruled from Constantinople.»
fact: Place names can change over time, so a city may have an old name and a new name.
fact: Tenochtitlan was the old name for the site of Mexico City, just as Constantinople was the old name for Istanbul.
exercise: «The empire was split into a western half ruled from Rome and an eastern half ruled from Constantinople.» Where was the eastern half ruled from? | Paris | *Constantinople | Mexico City | Rome
exercise: In which country is the city now called Istanbul? | Italy | Greece | *Turkey | Egypt
exercise: What does Constantinople mean? | A Roman emperor who ruled from Rome | *The old name of a great city now called Istanbul | A river in Mexico | A kind of castle
test: «Constantinople, later called Istanbul, became the Ottoman capital.» What does this sentence tell you? | Istanbul was never a capital | Constantinople is a type of food | *Istanbul was once called Constantinople | Istanbul is a village in Rome
test: Why might a game call the city Istanbul instead of Constantinople? | Constantinople is not a real place | Players cannot read old names | Istanbul is in Mexico | *Istanbul is the modern name used today
exam: The Ottoman sultan Mehmed II captured the city of ___ in 1453. | *Constantinople | Paris | Rome | Tenochtitlan
